as also found in LVGL's lv_lcd_st7701 driver (MIT). The register values are
transcribed, not the code.

Fonts (src/gui/fonts/)
----------------------
lv_font_montserrat_14_uml.c, _16_uml.c, _20_uml.c, _28_uml.c are generated with
LVGL's font converter from Montserrat Medium, SIL Open Font License 1.1. The
license text is next to them: src/gui/fonts/OFL-Montserrat.txt. The generator
command is in the header of each file; it adds the Latin-1 range (0xA0-0xFF) to
the ASCII set of the upstream font.

lv_font_portal_icons_20.c is generated the same way from `portal_icons.ttf`, a
subset that holds only the symbols the flow diagram uses. The generator command
is in the file's header. Where that symbol font came from is not recorded in
this repository — if it was taken from Google's Material Design Icons, then
Apache-2.0 applies to it. That should be settled before a binary is published
rather than after.

