Development-only dependency, not part of the firmware
----------------------------------------------------
tools/rct_sim.py and tools/rct_sim_test.py import the Python package `rctclient`
(GPL-3.0, https://github.com/svalouch/rctclient) for the frame codec, the
object-ID registry and the value tables. It runs on the build machine as a
separate process and is not redistributed with the firmware.

Protocol reference
------------------
The object IDs (rctOids[] in src/rct/RctClient.cpp) and the meaning of the 128
fault bits (src/i18n/Lang*.cpp) are facts about the device, taken from the
public documentation of the RCT Power Serial Communication Protocol.

The frame checksum in src/rct/RctCrc.h is an implementation of the published
CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE (polynomial 0x1021, preset 0xFFFF, MSB first) together with
the padding rule the device applies to odd-length frames. Its check values were
computed independently of the implementation and are checked in
tools/crc_test; a wrong checksum does not crash, it makes a healthy inverter
look unreachable, so it is worth a test of its own.

